  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Union support for resilient Mindanao</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Programme focuses on localizing a quadruple humanitarian-peace-climate-development (HPCD) nexus programme approach in communities that face multi-faceted and interlocking vulnerabilities. These communities are composed of Indigenous Peoples (IPs) , Internally Displaced People (IDPs) and those at risk of displacement, People with Disabilities (PWDs), women and girls, and youth  in Mindanao, especially in Geographically Isolated and Disadvantaged Areas (GIDAs) and in the Bangsamoro Autonomous Region in Muslim Mindanao (BARMM). Despite recent efforts to address persistent challenges in GIDAs and on implementing the Bangsamoro peace process, these groups have not fully benefitted from the resulting peace dividend due to persistent conflict, exposure to multiple hazards, engrained and longstanding discrimination, shortcomings in legal frameworks, and other sources of instability.  It champions a two-pronged approach: # Local communities# resiliency is increased (Outcome 1) and # Local value chains and value addition, fair production and economic opportunities for target communities are strengthened (Outcome 2). To operationalize the HPCD nexus, the human security approach   and conflict-sensitive programming across the two outcomes of the programme will be applied, ensuring programmatic coherence and cost-effec</narrative>
  </description>
